(199: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: %0A%23%23%20Context%0A%0AThe%20%22meta%22%20in%20meta-language%20%28issue%20%231%20%C2%A73.3%29%20requires%20the%20system%20to%20%2A%2Adescribe%0Aitself%20in%20its%20own%20terms%2A%2A%3A%20%60link%60%2C%20%60reference%60%2C%20%60relation%20link%60%2C%20%60language%60%2C%0A%60grammar%60%2C%20%60type%60%2C%20%60concept%60%2C%20%60point%60%2C%20%60field%60%2C%20%60trivia%60%2C%20%60region%60%2C%20%60object%60%20should%0Abe%20actual%20links%20whose%20definitions%20are%20written%20in%20those%20same%20terms.%20The%20README%20lists%0Athese%20roots%20and%20%60LinkMetadata%60%20has%20a%20%60definition%60%20field%2C%20but%20the%20roots%20are%20not%20yet%0Amaterialized%20as%20a%20seeded%20network.%20See%0A%5B%60requirements.md%60%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-language%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Fdocs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-3%2Frequirements.md%29%20CORE-8%2F9%20and%0A%5B%60ecosystem-foundations.md%60%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-language%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Fdocs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-3%2Fecosystem-foundations.md%29%20%28meta-theory%20definitions%29.%0A%0A%23%23%20Scope%0A%0A-%20Seed%20a%20self-description%20network%20where%20each%20root%20term%20is%20a%20link%20with%20a%0A%20%20%60definition%60%20written%20in%20the%20controlled%20vocabulary%20%28e.g.%20a%20%22point%22%20is%20defined%20as%20a%0A%20%20link%20that%20references%20only%20itself%20in%20every%20position%20%E2%80%94%20meta-theory%20line%20101%29.%0A-%20Seed%20the%20%22common%20roots%20of%20common%20ontologies%22%20from%20relative-meta-logic%27s%0A%20%20%60%28Type%3A%20Type%20Type%29%60%20self-referential%20root.%0A-%20Expose%20it%20via%20the%20existing%20%60describe%60%20CLI%20subcommand.%0A-%20Honor%20NFR-1%3A%20%22node%22%20%3D%20self-referential%20link%2C%20%22edge%22%20%3D%20connecting%20link%3B%20never%20the%0A%20%20word%20%22graph.%22%0A%0A%23%23%20Acceptance%20criteria%0A%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Each%20root%20term%20resolves%20to%20a%20link%20whose%20definition%20references%20only%20other%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20defined%20root%20links%20%28no%20undefined%20terms%3B%20no%20external%20vocabulary%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%60describe%60%20emits%20the%20self-description%20network%20and%20it%20round-trips%20losslessly.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20A%20test%20asserts%20the%20definition%20closure%20is%20complete%20%28every%20referenced%20term%20is%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20itself%20defined%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%60cargo%20test%20--all-features%60%20passes%3B%20changelog%20fragment%20%28%60bump%3A%20minor%60%29.%0A%0A%23%23%20References%0A%0A-%20Ecosystem%3A%20%5B%60ecosystem-foundations.md%60%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-language%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Fdocs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-3%2Fecosystem-foundations.md%29%20%28meta-theory%29%0A-%20Solution%3A%20%5B%60solution-plans.md%60%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-language%2Fblob%2Fmain%2Fdocs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-3%2Fsolution-plans.md%29%20Solution%208%0A-%20Requirements%3A%20CORE-8%2F9%0A%0A---%0A_Filed%20from%20%60docs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-3%2Fproposed-issues%2F12-self-description-roots.md%60.%20Part%20of%20the%20implementation%20plan%20for%20%233._%0A) (lang: meta-language%20structured%20data)))
